    {
      "id": "claim_2c8b3418eb1d4743bf68b94e9128d9a6",
      "statement": "Model selection must be distinguished from harness and gateway policy: decision models can handle frequent bounded choices while generative models propose candidates or perform extended reasoning, and workflow evaluation must account for prompts, tools, context packing, routing, costs, and fallback behavior rather than relying only on model or leaderboard scores.",
